{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1541198-working-on-a-d-d-style-fantasy-campaign-using-scion-as-a-base-ask-me-questions","id":1541198,"title":"Working on a D&D-style fantasy campaign using Scion as a base -- ask me questions!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-08-29T08:48:44-07:00","id":1541198,"title":"Working on a D&D-style fantasy campaign using Scion as a base -- ask me questions!","content":"I need grist for my brain mill for a project I'm working on, which is a D&amp;D-style Scion game turning Ye Olde Fantasy Pantheons into a workable setting. I'm aiming for a <i>Hercules: The Legendary Adventures/Xena: Warrior Princess</i> feel -- You know, &quot;this is the a story of a time long ago, an age of myth and legends&quot; sword and sorcery sort of game. I'm somewhat inspired by the Theros setting for D&amp;D/Magic The Gathering, but I'm using the pantheons from my own homebrew campaign setting rather than any pre-built ones.<br /> <br /> The Pantheons I'm planning on having available in the setting are as follows:<ul><li><b>The Nine Heroes</b>: The Nine Heroes were mortals who gained the power of the Gods performing legendary deeds in order to challenge The Seven, who were the cruel and tyrannical God-Kings of The Three Worlds (the Prime Material Plane, The Shadowfell, and The Feywild, for those of you who know D&amp;D cosmology). Today, they serves as exemplars and champions of the mortal races, inspiring them to strive for greatness now that the tyranny of The Seven is at an end. This means they are actively promoting and supporting Scions, which will (eventually) lead to problems -- this game is set in the ancient history of my campaign world, during a time before the gods separated themselves from mortalkind into your more traditional D&amp;D setting, and the build-up of trouble (ending in something called &quot;The Godswar&quot;) is what convinced them they needed to do this to preserve the world.</li> <li><b>The Seven Devils</b>: These serve as The Titans of the setting, the Seven created the mortal races, destroyed the singular Perfect World that once existed, and rebuilt reality into the imperfect Three Worlds that currently exist in the center of Creation. They each are considered to have &quot;Fallen&quot; from grace when they took on their Titanic Mantles, and grew ever more corrupt and destructive before The Nine Heroes rose to challenge their dominance. They are currently trapped, though they can have less direct influence on the world through their Scions. This is one of the primarily antagonistic factions -- there's still a lot of mortals who are convinced The Nine and the mortal races should not have turned on their rightful rulers, and there's a distinct current of &quot;The Fallen shall rise again&quot; sentiment, mostly among people and cultures that feel they're disadvantaged in the new order of things.</li> <li><b>The Tempest Djinn</b>: The Tempest Djinn are a contracting pantheon -- they were locked away by The Seven and freed by The Nine, so they have some gratitude there, but they're more elemental deities that remember The Perfect World and want to reclaim what was lost, which can bring them into conflict with the current order. The Tempest Djinn are gods of the elements in a way that the Nine aren't but they're not quite Primordial in their distance from human affairs, so they sort of serve the role of Dragons in divine politics.</li> <li><b>The Old Gods</b>: The Old Gods are The Primordials of the setting -- the ones who made all of greater Creation and fashioned the original Perfect World that The Seven ruled and then broke. They don't really care much about mortal affairs, though one of them can be said to be a Titan who has even stronger chains on it than The Seven do, as it's the primordial expression of entropy and the eventual destruction of everything. The Old Gods comprise the forces of Creation, Destruction, Time (and, to a certain extent, Order), Life (and, to a certain extent, Chaos), and Souls (think of the element of &quot;Heart&quot; from Captain Planet). Scions of these entities would be rare, but they're an important part of the background mythology.</li> <li><b>The Stars of Ill-Omen</b>: These are the eldritch Mythos-style entities of the setting, a collection of sentient stars and other celestial object that have a comprehension of how long eternity is, are trapped knowing they are slowly dying, fear that slow, endless march to oblivion, and want to speed it up, either by forcing their own ends or the end of everything in creation. They don't care about mortals, not really, but mortals can do things they can't, so they aren't indifferent to them either, and scheme to use mortal pawns to aid them reach their apocalyptic goals. I've mentioned them on these boards before in passing.</li> <li><b>The Demon Princes</b>: The final faction, one I don't plan on offering as player options but as strictly an antagonistic force, are the Demon Princes of The Abyss, a large crack in reality that was made by the Titan of Destruction's first serious stab at ending everything. Demons are a scourge that seek to break, ruin, corrupt, and defile all of reality, burning it to the ground so they can dance on its ashes until they're reabsorbed by Cacophony (the aforementioned Titan). The Seven might have a point about being the true rulers, and they aren't completely hostile to all existence --- they want to rule, not destroy. The Demon princes want to destroy, and they don't want just physical destruction but conceptual and moral destruction as well. They are what you can point to as &quot;pure evil&quot; in the setting.</li> </ul>I have stuff done, but I've reached a point where I have a lot of ideas swimming around and not a lot of direction. I find that answering questions helps me define things easier, so I'm requesting help. Ask me questions! Ask me anything you want about the setting, what sorts of changes I'm doing, any meta questions you'd like insight on, or anything else, and I'll do my best to answer them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When the cat's a Stray, the mice will pray...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25851-thestray7","name":"TheStray7","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25851_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-07T01:38:22-07:00","id":1541680,"title":"","content":"How is this going to be played? Is it a game of Scion?<br /> Are the Heroes, Devils. Djinn, Old Gods, Stars and Demons intended to be separate 'pantheons' mechanically?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-07T05:20:29-07:00","id":1541682,"title":"","content":"How are you handling wizard types? Powers Scion has, but the flexible lists of spells not so much. Have you thought of bringing in Sphere magic from Mage: The Ascension or C:tD Realms and Arts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-08T20:19:42-07:00","id":1541761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1541198-working-on-a-d-d-style-fantasy-campaign-using-scion-as-a-base-ask-me-questions?p=1541680#post1541680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How is this going to be played? Is it a game of Scion?<br /> Are the Heroes, Devils. Djinn, Old Gods, Stars and Demons intended to be separate 'pantheons' mechanically?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the intention, though I'm thinking of converting the base system to Storypath Ultra as more of it gets revealed (and will eagerly be looking forward to any conversion tips they present as the campaign goes on).<br /> <br /> The Nine are going to have a specialized Pantheon Path that has 5 different branches to represent the stock fantasy archetypes (based on the archetypes from Exalted Essence -- Warrior, Priest, Savant, Trickster and Broker). Each Path has different skills, but share a general ethos, Virtues, and Motif. The Pantheon Specialized Purview is like a Specialized Purview -- slightly more limited, but each path grants access to a Boon unique to it (though there are, like normal, some overarching boons availibe to anyone who takes the PSP).<br /> <br /> The Stars have some similarities to the Mythos, though I'm mostly harvesting Knacks to make new Callings rather than using corrupted versions of the existing ones. I haven't decided if I want to use Dragon Heir mechanics for the Djinn yet, or just keep it simple. The Seven are Titans, though there are echoes of their less monstrous Divine Mantles that can be found in the setting if someone wants to try &quot;redeeming&quot; them -- they have similarities with the Annuna in design. The Old Gods are mostly Primordials, though I'm planning on having some options to play Scions of theirs if someone really wants to.<br /> <br /> The Demons are the odd ones out -- they are an overtly villainous Pantheon, not suitable for PC play. They're mostly going to be represented by various flavors of Titanspawn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When the cat's a Stray, the mice will pray...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25851-thestray7","name":"TheStray7","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25851_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-08T20:33:06-07:00","id":1541762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1541198-working-on-a-d-d-style-fantasy-campaign-using-scion-as-a-base-ask-me-questions?p=1541682#post1541682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How are you handling wizard types? Powers Scion has, but the flexible lists of spells not so much. Have you thought of bringing in Sphere magic from Mage: The Ascension or C:tD Realms and Arts?</div> </div> </div> </div>I plan to use the Sorcery system from Saints &amp; Monsters, actually, since that fits with the feel I want to go for. I also plan on having the Magic Purview for those who want to dip their toes into Sorcery without committing fully. I might work out some sort of &quot;Vancian&quot; Motif or Power Source to more fully capture the original flavor of D&amp;D magic, but I'm not going full Sphere Magick -- that's just too much conversion work. This is a Scion game with D&amp;D elements, not a D&amp;D game with Scion elements.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When the cat's a Stray, the mice will pray...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25851-thestray7","name":"TheStray7","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25851_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-15T16:29:51-07:00","id":1542208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheStray7</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1541198-working-on-a-d-d-style-fantasy-campaign-using-scion-as-a-base-ask-me-questions?p=1541761#post1541761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> *snip* <br /> <br /> The Nine are going to have a specialized Pantheon Path that has 5 different branches to represent the stock fantasy archetypes (based on the archetypes from Exalted Essence -- Warrior, Priest, Savant, Trickster and Broker). Each Path has different skills, but share a general ethos, Virtues, and Motif. The Pantheon Specialized Purview is like a Specialized Purview -- slightly more limited, but each path grants access to a Boon unique to it (though there are, like normal, some overarching boons availibe to anyone who takes the PSP).<br /> <br /> *snip*</div> </div> </div> </div>This strikes me as odd. Those roles are represented in Scion as Callings, though they can also be Paths. Scion by default does have Role paths, though SPU does not. Some are easier to follow than others, (Warrior &amp; Trickster are literal Callings, Sage &amp; Creator resemble Exalted's Savants, Leader &amp; Lover fulfill the same 'face' role of the Broker), with only Priest left in the cold. Which given the role of a Scion (to act as an intermediary between the mundane &amp; Divine) is also part of the job of a Priest, there is a reason why the base game of Scion doesn't really have them.<br /> Though one could argue that Saints &amp; Prophets sort of fit the role of the Preist Archetype.<br /> <br /> I guess I am just confused that there are tools in the system that you don't seem to be using, in favor of trying to reinvent the wheel.<br /> <br /> I should point out the role of Dragons in Scion as the 'third party side' is not mechanically supported, so you don't need to make Djinn different to have them 'slot in'. Except for some Birthrights but just saying &quot;Djinn Scions can take these Birthrights&quot; solves that quite quickly.<br /> Heirs' mechanical differences result in slowly turning into a lizard monster with a very different magic system. Dragon spells are not the same or even compatible to Purview &amp; Sorcery. By RAW Relics don't provide access to Dragon Magic and raiding a Hoard won't provide Purview access. This would be an easy fix...if there is a one-to-one equivalent between the Magic and Purviews. <br /> Not sure if it is fit for your purposes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-25T06:14:30-07:00","id":1542625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1541198-working-on-a-d-d-style-fantasy-campaign-using-scion-as-a-base-ask-me-questions?p=1542208#post1542208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This strikes me as odd. Those roles are represented in Scion as Callings, though they can also be Paths. Scion by default does have Role paths, though SPU does not. Some are easier to follow than others, (Warrior &amp; Trickster are literal Callings, Sage &amp; Creator resemble Exalted's Savants, Leader &amp; Lover fulfill the same 'face' role of the Broker), with only Priest left in the cold. Which given the role of a Scion (to act as an intermediary between the mundane &amp; Divine) is also part of the job of a Priest, there is a reason why the base game of Scion doesn't really have them.<br /> Though one could argue that Saints &amp; Prophets sort of fit the role of the Priest Archetype.<br /> <br /> I guess I am just confused that there are tools in the system that you don't seem to be using, in favor of trying to reinvent the wheel.</div> </div> </div> </div>Callings don't provide any Skill Points to make people actually <i>good</i> at the Calling skills. Sticking with one Path for the Nine means the player is stuck with points in skills that they might not necessarily <i>want</i>. The Nine are supposed to be mortalkind's Exemplars, the people who were so good at their chosen vocation they could challenge the gods themselves and win, so the 5 Paths are meant to allow for that while giving variety (since I'm not creating a whole bunch of Pantheons to choose from like normal Scion has). Priest, by the way, has elements of the Judge and Shepherd callings, though you're right that Saints have some pull there. Prophets would be split between Savant and Priest.<br /> <br /> So think of it this way -- the Paths of Heroes is meant more as a overall cultural focus on Being a Hero, while the Callings complement them (or draw them in a different direction, if you pick Callings at odds with your Path). Each of the Nine represent two of the Paths, representing what they are seen as the Exemplars <i>of</i>. There's also one pairing that is left over, which could potentially be picked up by someone in the future as a &quot;tenth&quot; member.<br /> <br /> This is even more important, by the way, if I decided to use Storypath Ultra's approach to Paths, which grants fewer overall Skill Points to players at character creation. If I want players to be good at the various archetypal roles, they need to have the Skill Points to actually be so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I should point out the role of Dragons in Scion as the 'third party side' is not mechanically supported, so you don't need to make Djinn different to have them 'slot in'. Except for some Birthrights but just saying &quot;Djinn Scions can take these Birthrights&quot; solves that quite quickly.<br /> Heirs' mechanical differences result in slowly turning into a lizard monster with a very different magic system. Dragon spells are not the same or even compatible to Purview &amp; Sorcery. By RAW Relics don't provide access to Dragon Magic and raiding a Hoard won't provide Purview access. This would be an easy fix...if there is a one-to-one equivalent between the Magic and Purviews.<br /> Not sure if it is fit for your purposes. </div> </div> </div>I haven't really decided how tied I am to having the Djinn being mechanically a &quot;third party&quot; or how much I want to use the &quot;we become dragons&quot; detail of Heirs, just as I'm not sure I'm going to focus on the difference between Legend and Awareness for Scions of the Stars of Ill-Omen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When the cat's a Stray, the mice will pray...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25851-thestray7","name":"TheStray7","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25851_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}